
“Using remote file access, transfer files to the VM using FTP, initialize the Git repository and push to GitHub.”

You have already created a GitHub repository named `storage`, so we will use that same repository. We will follow the order: create a file on Windows → transfer it to Ubuntu using FileZilla → initialize Git → push to GitHub → clone the repository.

# Step 1: Create a file on Windows

Open Windows PowerShell (not Ubuntu Terminal).

Run these commands one by one:

```
mkdir storage
cd storage
```

Create a sample text file:

```
Set-Content storage.txt "This is my remote storage file."
```

Check the file:

```
dir
```

You should see:

```
storage.txt
```

# Step 2: Prepare Ubuntu for remote file access

Open your Ubuntu VM and run:

```
sudo apt update
```

Install SSH:

```
sudo apt install openssh-server -y
```

Start SSH:

```
sudo systemctl enable --now ssh
```

Check SSH status:

```
sudo systemctl status ssh
```

Press `q` to exit the status screen.

Find your Ubuntu username:

```
whoami
```

Find your Ubuntu IP address:

```
hostname -I
```

Note down the IP address. You will need it in FileZilla.

# Step 3: Connect Windows to Ubuntu using FileZilla

