[owlhowto.com](https://owlhowto.com/how-to-install-filezilla-in-debian-12/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

1. Open FileZilla on Windows.
2. Enter these details:

| Field    | Value                                |
| -------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Protocol | SFTP - SSH File Transfer Protocol    |
| Host     | Ubuntu IP address from `hostname -I` |
| Username | Ubuntu username from `whoami`        |
| Password | Your Ubuntu login password           |
| Port     | `22`                                 |

3. Click Quickconnect.
4. Accept the SSH host-key confirmation if it appears.

On the right side, open your Ubuntu home directory:

```
/home/your-ubuntu-username/
```

On the left side, open the Windows `storage` folder.

Drag `storage.txt` from the left side to the right side.

Transfer complete

Your file is now transferred to Ubuntu.

# Step 4: Organize the transferred file in Ubuntu

Open Ubuntu Terminal and run:

```
mkdir -p ~/storage
mv ~/storage.txt ~/storage/
cd ~/storage
```

Check the file:

```
ls
cat storage.txt
```

You should see your file and its contents.

# Step 5: Install Git

```
sudo apt install git -y
```

Check Git installation:

```
git --version
```

Configure your Git identity. Use your own name and GitHub email:

```
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@gmail.com"
```

# Step 6: Initialize the Git repository

Make sure you are inside the `storage` folder:

```
cd ~/storage
```

Initialize Git:

```
git init
```

Add the files:

```
git add .
```

Commit the files:

```
git commit -m "Initial commit"
```

Set the branch name:

```
git branch -M main
```

# Step 7: Connect your existing GitHub repository

Your repository name is `storage`.

Run this command after replacing `YOUR-USERNAME` with your GitHub username:

```
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/storage.git
```

Check the remote:

```
git remote -v
```

Push your files to GitHub:

```
git push -u origin main
```

GitHub upload complete

Open your GitHub `storage` repository and refresh the page. You should see `storage.txt`.


# Step 8: Clone the GitHub repository

Now download the repository into a separate folder in Ubuntu.

```
cd ~
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/storage.git
```

Enter the cloned repository:

```
cd storage
```

Check the files:

```
ls
```

Read the file:

```
cat storage.txt
```

Check Git status:

```
git status
```

# Step 9: Test GitHub synchronization

Make a small change:

```
echo "Updated from Ubuntu VM." >> storage.txt
```

Add and commit:

```
git add .
git commit -m "Updated storage file"
```

Push the update:

```
git push
```

Pull the latest version:

```
git pull origin main
```


1. Create `storage.txt` on Windows.
2. Connect FileZilla to Ubuntu using SFTP.
3. Transfer `storage.txt` to Ubuntu.
4. Initialize Git using `git init`.
5. Commit the file using `git add` and `git commit`.
6. Push the file to your existing GitHub `storage` repository.
7. Clone the repository and verify the downloaded file.

